Four groups that are a pure function of the parameter snapshot left the
function for headers of their own: the tape formula and the instrument
selector's voicing, the device couplings, the two glue stages' operating
points, and the delay head's time. processTapeEngine() was 1,547 lines when
the pass began and is 1,210 now.

No rendered-audio harness reaches processTapeEngine() itself, so the moved
code is kept honest from both sides: tests/dsp/subfund_test.cpp calls the
shipping headers directly, and check_headers_juce.sh compiles them against
real JUCE. That second check matters because the shim has been answering
juce::jlimit and juce::jmax for years, and a name the shim provides is not
proof that JUCE provides it.

The line numbers in SPLITTING-BIG-FILES.md and docs/architecture.md are
re-measured from the function rather than adjusted by the size of the diff.

