From f677a07e180e3633c9c97e60fe613b9102de7345 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mihalera <88746771+mihalera@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:13:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] The front panel remembers the theme and the USER palette
 across an editor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A host that destroys and re-creates the editor dropped a desk left on USER back
onto IVORY and lost the palette the COLOURS window had been editing. Both are
preferences of the same kind as the renderer choice, so they are stored beside
it: the theme by NAME, because an enum insertion cannot then silently select a
different panel, and the palette through the field table UserThemeWindow.h
already owns.

WHITE MONSTER returns to the THEME cycle, and both translations name it, so the
cycle the tooltip promises and the cycle the button walks are the same one.

🤖 Generated with Codebuff
Co-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
